{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1634, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a string s consisting of digits. Perform the following operation repeatedly until the string has exactly two digits:\n\nFor each pair of consecutive digits in s, starting from the first digit, calculate a new digit as the sum of the two digits modulo 10.\nReplace s with the sequence of newly calculated digits, maintaining the order in which they are computed.\n\nReturn true if the final two digits in s are the same; otherwise, return false.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"3902\"\nOutput: true\nExplanation:\n\nInitially, s = \"3902\"\nFirst operation:\n\t\n(s[0] + s[1]) % 10 = (3 + 9) % 10 = 2\n(s[1] + s[2]) % 10 = (9 + 0) % 10 = 9\n(s[2] + s[3]) % 10 = (0 + 2) % 10 = 2\ns becomes \"292\"\n\n\nSecond operation:\n\t\n(s[0] + s[1]) % 10 = (2 + 9) % 10 = 1\n(s[1] + s[2]) % 10 = (9 + 2) % 10 = 1\ns becomes \"11\"\n\n\nSince the digits in \"11\" are the same, the output is true.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"34789\"\nOutput: false\nExplanation:\n\nInitially, s = \"34789\".\nAfter the first operation, s = \"7157\".\nAfter the second operation, s = \"862\".\nAfter the third operation, s = \"48\".\nSince '4' != '8', the output is false.\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n3 <= s.length <= 100\ns consists of only digits.\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def hasSameDigits(self, s: str) -> bool:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1672, "char_start": 1646, "quote": "Input:\n\"3902\"\nOutput:\ntrue", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1712, "char_start": 1684, "quote": "Input:\n\"34789\"\nOutput:\nfalse", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "60d607eb2057b6012b2453a89049cd2b0d004342b709652a747c050d6b19ce1d", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "6ac9bc52058c760b561721105933ab8f22dc6d5d447d59165e7218be3bf3f9a9", "seq": 2}
